eye-contact-co-processing-at-the-speed-of-light-lines-4 : List (List Word)
eye-contact-co-processing-at-the-speed-of-light-lines-4 = cons "## 1. Your Brain Is Exposed to the World" (cons "" (cons "Embryologically, the human retina is not a peripheral sensor wired to the brain after the fact—it develops directly from the diencephalic neuroectoderm as an outgrowth of the optic vesicle. The retina is central nervous system tissue positioned at the surface of the body." (cons "" (cons "Through the transparent cornea and crystalline lens, incoming electromagnetic radiation strikes roughly 126 million photoreceptors (approximately 120 million rods and 6 million cones) arranged as a dense spatial array, compressed through roughly one million retinal ganglion cell axons per optic nerve straight into the lateral geniculate nucleus, primary visual cortex, superior colliculus, pulvinar, and amygdala. When light enters your eye, the external world is interacting directly with exposed central nervous tissue." (cons "" nil)))))
